# EXPONENTIAL field-chain typing, LONG-STANDING (measured 2026-09-17).
#
# A chain rooted at a REFERENCE parameter whose links RESOLVE: 28 links take ~23s, and every
# two further links multiply the cost by ~4. The Sep-12 product is worse still (>45s), so this
# one is NOT a regression -- it is latent and has never been gated.
#
# Why the Aug-26 guard in resolve_types_infer.elisa does not stop it: that guard bails only when
# the object is a Field whose COARSE type came back Unknown. Here every link resolves through the
# structural channel, so the coarse kind is Named, the guard never fires, and the Field arm walks
# `object` TWICE -- once via infer_expression_type and again via structural_type_id_of -- at every
# level. The guard's own comment reasons about the FIRST link only ("field access through a
# reference parameter is an Ident, not a Field"); from the second link on, the object IS a Field
# and the premise no longer holds.
struct Node:
    b: Node&

def f(a: Node&) -> i64:
    _ = a.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b
    return 0
